    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'formula' has several common meanings, including a mathematical rule (e.g., E=mc²), a recipe/composition (e.g., baby formula), and a method/system. The Japanese expression '方式' (houshiki) primarily covers the 'method, system, form' sense of formula. It does not naturally cover the mathematical or recipe senses, for which '公式' (koushiki) and '処方' (shohou) or 'レシピ' (reshipi) would be more appropriate, respectively. Given the 'general, daily_life' domain and 'core-formula' concept, '方式' is too narrow as it misses the very common mathematical meaning of 'formula'. A learner expecting the mathematical sense would find '方式' unnatural and incorrect.",
