      "surface": "公式",
      "reading": "こうしき",
      "reason": "'公式' (koushiki) is the standard and most natural Japanese term for a mathematical or scientific 'formula', which is a core meaning of the English lemma. It also has senses related to 'formality' or 'official method', making it a better general fit than '方式' for the broader concept of 'formula'."
    }
